[H4] ISOSTATIC: #lonely clocks of the AP = φ(n) (the unit orbit) = the critical count
  n | φ(n) | #lonely | binding/lonely-clock | over-rigid (0 lonely) possible?
   6 |    2 |       2 |  2 (v with vj≡±1)        | NO — orbit floor φ(n)=2>0 forbids it
   7 |    6 |       6 |  2 (v with vj≡±1)        | NO — orbit floor φ(n)=6>0 forbids it
  10 |    4 |       4 |  2 (v with vj≡±1)        | NO — orbit floor φ(n)=4>0 forbids it
  13 |   12 |      12 |  2 (v with vj≡±1)        | NO — orbit floor φ(n)=12>0 forbids it
  14 |    6 |       6 |  2 (v with vj≡±1)        | NO — orbit floor φ(n)=6>0 forbids it
  18 |    6 |       6 |  2 (v with vj≡±1)        | NO — orbit floor φ(n)=6>0 forbids it
  22 |   10 |      10 |  2 (v with vj≡±1)        | NO — orbit floor φ(n)=10>0 forbids it
  => the worry-set (AP) is CRITICALLY rigid: exactly φ(n) witnesses, 2 binders each
     (isostatic). A counterexample = 0 witnesses = over-rigid, below the orbit floor φ(n).

[H6] RIGIDITY-HEIGHT = v2(n): doubling x->2x nilpotency index on the 2-part Z/2^a
  n | v2(n) | doubling-nilpotency on 2-part | height interpretation
   7 |    0  |                        0      | 0 — odd, no 2-adic break (prime-regular)
  13 |    0  |                        0      | 0 — odd, no 2-adic break (prime-regular)
  14 |    1  |                        1      | 1 — 1 break(s) above the prime; n=14 is height 1
  10 |    1  |                        1      | 1 — 1 break(s) above the prime; n=14 is height 1
  22 |    1  |                        1      | 1 — 1 break(s) above the prime; n=14 is height 1
  28 |    2  |                        2      | 2 — 2 break(s) above the prime; n=14 is height 1
   8 |    3  |                        3      | 3 — 3 break(s) above the prime; n=14 is height 1
  16 |    4  |                        4      | 4 — 4 break(s) above the prime; n=14 is height 1
  56 |    3  |                        3      | 3 — 3 break(s) above the prime; n=14 is height 1
  => rigidity-height = v2(n): each doubling level degrades the dynamical rigidity by one
     factor of 2; n=14=2·7 has height 1 (the single mod-2 collapse = the apex/2-adic seam).
